<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:53Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Bulgaria seeks suspects in Germany after Starlink sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c9952c379e5e7e785525550251ed813b4c15d51abc2ac1f498e12da5da41420</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T18:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745--e11bc2352fd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Bulgarian court has issued arrest warrants for two young German nationals suspected of setting fire to Starlink antennas. The case is reminiscent of another in Poland, which Warsaw says was orchestrated by Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Emergency at Leipzig airport sparked by novice driver</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f05e5a85ce669159d5a72245bf8e1094685276fcbc5d733f5667e30932649b23</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T17:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-emergency-at-leipzig-airport-sparked-by-novice-driver/live-79695354--1d0844a30c8b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-emergency-at-leipzig-airport-sparked-by-novice-driver/live-79695354?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two men breached a fence at the Leipzig/Halle airport while practicing for a driving test. Meanwhile, German Chancellor Friedrich Merz announced an industrial AI partnership with Nvidia. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Police probe security incident at Leipzig/Halle airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f7af483561d79e22bbf87e5fa4a7a57cdfcb607b245e08138c446a99397ea73d</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-probe-security-incident-at-leipzig-halle-airport/live-79686913--f152414b1a9b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-probe-security-incident-at-leipzig-halle-airport/live-79686913?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fence breach at the Leipzig/Halle airport has triggered a major police operation. And, Christian Social Union leader Markus Söder calls for a "firewall" against leftists at a conservative youth conference.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is Germany's eight-hour workday under threat?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1449fc1d80b906d2beb82651ce98fc279263db2dfad8a849bcdb7bf60762f5c</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T10:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-eight-hour-workday-under-threat/a-79680984--28b0ad264d5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-eight-hour-workday-under-threat/a-79680984?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Would you work 12 hours straight? The CDU/CSU and SPD are locked in a dispute over reforms to the Working Hours Act. Workplace flexibility, collective bargaining agreements and worker protection rules are at stake.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>How big is Russia's threat against Germany?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b45ad8b9c15cd91f73fb8c49c28f3f846096118dd52be8b024dccec7b4dae1d</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T15:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-big-is-russia-s-threat-against-germany/a-79688426--e8db9669a70a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-big-is-russia-s-threat-against-germany/a-79688426?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Experts believe that, so far, Germany has been ill-prepared — both militarily and mentally — for Russian provocations. They also warn against the idea that ending support for Ukraine would make Germany safer.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>'Ragebait' is the 2026 German Youth Word of the Year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:224f082c59f6fe29f2c649ce513f9dada024dbce3912240b212e6fcb1bca78ac</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158--c39c4c350c71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Already named the 2025 Oxford Word of the Year, "rage bait" has also been widely adopted in German slang.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Author or artificial intelligence? Literature in crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2982cfff49673da22c8690a6a13a8e5e149cbe8c5135dcf1fab0e65936f303c</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610--2ddbca94bc5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI is a hot topic at this year's Frankfurt Book Fair. An international literary scandal has raised questions about machine-generated texts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
